        "Key squares are the squares whose occupation by the king guarantees promotion. For a pawn on the 4th there are three (for d4: c6, d6, e6), for a pawn on the 5th — six. A rook pawn is the exception. Do not confuse this with the square rule, and do not push the pawn before occupying a key square.",
